{"id": "EUVD-2026-103063", "enisaUuid": "e46f2e20-2334-386e-a231-c735d1cee290", "description": "FastapiAdmin through 3.0 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to obtain sessions for any user by abusing unprotected auto-login endpoints. Attackers can list users via /api/v1/auth/auto-login/users, mint a superuser auto-login token, and exchange it for a JWT session to gain full administrative control.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:18:51", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/fastapiadmin-unauthenticated-autologin-and-hardcoded-jwt-secret", "https://github.com/fastapiadmin/FastapiAdmin/blob/v3.0/backend/app/api/v1/module_system/auth/controller.py#L173-L251", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fastapiadmin-through-3.0-authentication-bypass-via-auto-login-endpoints"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111641", "GHSA-xj6f-6mc4-xhqp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "42e98aee-bdab-3a6c-9a16-6e2032cf7629", "product": {"name": "FastApiAdmin", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9f2d1115-8fc1-38be-b7e7-330ce45208fe", "vendor": {"name": "fastapiadmin"}}], "isExploited": false}